    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "You were saying \"is like trying...\" and then it cut off. But I get the minefield thing. It's just that these risks don't feel like big, obvious landmines. They feel more like these tiny, chaotic, little things that hide in the dark corners of the contract just waiting to cause trouble the moment you aren't looking. If you had to use a metaphor for that specific kind of small, mischievous, hidden trouble, what would it be?",
      "source": "evaluator",
